18The👤 centurion🪖 brought🚶 him👦 to➡️ the👤 commander🪖 and🔗 said🗣️, “Paul🙋 the⛓️ prisoner⛓️ called📣 me🙋 over➡️ and🔗 asked🙏 me🙋 to➡️ bring🚶 this💯 young👦 man👦 to➡️ you🫵. He👤 has✅ a💯 message📨 for➡️ you🫵.”
19The👤 commander🪖 took🤝 the👦 young👦 man👦 by➡️ the🤝 hand🤝, pulled🤲 him👦 aside↗️ privately🤫, and🔗 asked❓, “What💬 do✅ you🫵 need💭 to➡️ tell🗣️ me🙋?”
20He👦 said🗣️, “Some💯 Jews✡️ agreed🤝 to➡️ ask🙏 you🫵 to➡️ bring🚶 Paul🙋 before➡️ the🏛️ council🧑‍⚖️ tomorrow📆, pretending🎭 they🫂 need💭 to➡️ question❓ him🙋 more➕ carefully🔎.
21Don’t🚫 go🚫 along➡️ with➡️ them🫂, because💡 over➡️ forty🔢 men👥 are✅ waiting⏳ in📍 ambush🪤. They👥 made✅ an💯 oath🤞 not🚫 to➡️ eat🍽️ or🔀 drink🥤 until⏳ they👥 kill💀 him🙋. Unu🫵, they👥 are✅ ready💪 right⏱️ now⏱️, just💯 waiting⏳ for➡️ your👤 yes✅.”
22The👤 commander🪖 let💨 the👦 young👦 man👦 go🚶 and🔗 warned⚠️ him🙋, “Don’t🚫 tell🗣️ anybody👤 you🫵 reported📨 this💯 to➡️ me🙋.”
23Then🔜 he👤 called📣 two🔢 centurions🪖 and🔗 said🗣️, “Get💪 two🔢 hundred💯 soldiers🪖 ready💪 to➡️ go🚶 to➡️ Caesarea🏙️, plus➕ seventy🔢 horsemen🐎 and🔗 two🔢 hundred💯 spearmen🛡️. Move🚶 out➡️ at📍 the💯 third🕒 hour🕒 of➡️ the🌙 night🌙—unu🫵, get💪 this💯 unit🪖 moving🚶.”
24“Get🐎 horses🐎 too💯, so💡 Paul🙋 can✅ ride🐎 safely🛟 to➡️ Governor👑 Felix👑.”
25He👤 wrote✍️ a💯 letter✉️ like💭 this💡:
